women in Brazil make a chipa of corn, too."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"Gastronomica, Making chipas in Paraguay","url":"https://gastronomica.org/2009/05/04/making-chipas-paraguay/"},{"name":"Slow Food Foundation, Ark of Taste, Guarani Mbya bolo de milho","url":"https://www.fondazioneslowfood.com/en/ark-of-taste-slow-food/guarani-mbya-bolo-de-milho/"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-chipa"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chip%C3%A1"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Guaraní foodways","cuisine/guarani-foodways"],["Paraguayan cuisine","cuisine/paraguayan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":6,"links":[["Anise","ingredient/anise"],["Cassava","ingredient/cassava"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Lard","ingredient/lard"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Camila Made: Top 15 Paraguayan Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"camilamade.com","note":"Paraguayan recipe roundup on a Latin American home cooking blog.","url":"https://camilamade.com/top-15-paraguayan-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/9e/Chipa_Paraguay.jpg/500px-Chipa_Paraguay.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Ekem at English Wikipedia","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chipa_Paraguay.jpg"}}}